# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Phase 16 added Windows and Linux to the build matrix. Without this, a Windows checkout
# with the default `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites every text file to CRLF on the way out,
# and the golden fixtures both products compare byte-for-byte — address_reference.json,
# geo_directory_reference.json, the contract schemas, the catalogue seed — stop matching.
# That failure looks like a data bug and is a checkout bug.
* text=auto eol=lf

# HL7 v2 messages are exempt from normalisation, because in v2 the carriage return is not a
# line ending — it is the segment separator, defined as such by the standard. `text=auto` exists
# to rewrite line endings, and a format where CR is data is precisely where that must not
# happen. The reference corpus is compared byte-for-byte by
# `app/scripts/generate-reference-corpus.ts --check`, so a checkout that rewrote separators
# would fail the gate on Windows and look like an exporter bug.
*.hl7     -text

# Binary, never touched.
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.ico     binary
*.icns    binary
*.pdf     binary
*.docx    binary
*.xlsx    binary
*.gz      binary
*.zip     binary
*.tgz     binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.db      binary
*.bak-*   binary
